kunsten_be_flanders_1c78c30f66d3,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-support-by-the-netherlands-embassy-in-belgium/,https://dutchculture.nl/en/news/open-call-support-dutch-embassy-brussels,Netherlands Embassy in Belgium,"Every year, the Netherlands Embassy in Belgium organises several open calls for funding support for all disciplines.","all disciplines; performing arts, contemporary visual arts, the creative industries (especially architecture, design, fashion and digital art), and cultural heritage",open calls for funding support,Belgium,,funding support,,,en,Open call for support by the Netherlands Embassy in Belgium,"Eligible for support are Dutch-Belgian co-projects across all disciplines, but special attention is given to the performing arts, contemporary visual arts, the creative industries (especially architecture, design, fashion and digital art), and cultural heritage. Multidisciplinary projects are also welcome. In addition, the embassy welcomes projects that explore innovative formats and presentation methods, cross-border cultural exchange, and initiatives that promote participation and inclusion, equal rights, and sustainability. Projects must take place in Belgium, unless they involve virtual collaboration. Special attention is given to projects taking place in Wallonia and the Meuse-Rhine Euregion. Note: only the Belgian partner can apply for this funding.",Open call for support by the Netherlands Embassy in Belgium,"Eligible for support are Dutch-Belgian co-projects across all disciplines, but special attention is given to the performing arts, contemporary visual arts, the creative industries (especially architecture, design, fashion and digital art), and cultural heritage. Multidisciplinary projects are also welcome. In addition, the embassy welcomes projects that explore innovative formats and presentation methods, cross-border cultural exchange, and initiatives that promote participation and inclusion, equal rights, and sustainability. Projects must take place in Belgium, unless they involve virtual collaboration. Special attention is given to projects taking place in Wallonia and the Meuse-Rhine Euregion. Note: only the Belgian partner can apply for this funding.",3 November 2026,2026-11-03,2026-09-23 12:37:25.034997+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_1e4f87dbc5b9,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/visualise-support-for-international-exhibition-projects-with-ukrainian-partners/,https://ui.org.ua/en/news-en/visualise-2026-international-exhibition-support-programme/,Ukrainian Institute,"A long-term programme by the Ukrainian Institute aimed at supporting exhibition projects outside of Ukraine. The programme provides opportunities of co-programming, co-financing, and communications support to international exhibitions that contribute to promoting the art of Ukraine globally and establishing institutional partnerships.",Art exhibitions,open call,Ukraine,,"The maximum financing per project is up to 1,500,000.00 UAH.",,,en,Visualise – support for international exhibition projects with Ukrainian partners,"The following entities are eligible to apply: legal bodies of all forms of ownership and private entrepreneurs registered in Ukraine with a confirmed prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one; organisations and companies registered outside of Ukraine, their branch offices and delegations registered and certified in Ukraine with a confirmed institutional capacity and prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one.

Applications submitted by individuals, legal entities registered both in Ukraine and abroad, related to the aggressor state – the Russian Federation, which is recognized as such in accordance with the Law of Ukraine“ “On the Prohibition of Propaganda of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime, Armed Aggression of the Russian Federation as a Terrorist State against Ukraine, Symbolism of the Military Invasion of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime into Ukraine”№ 2265-ІХ of May 22, 2022, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran, are considered ineligible, namely: legal entities with beneficiaries who are individuals – citizens of the aggressor state of the Russian Federation, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran or or legal entities associated with the aggressor state of the Russian Federation and the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran; legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities to whom personal special economic and other restrictive measures (sanctions) have been applied in accordance with the Law of Ukraine “On Sanctions” and decisions of the National Security and Defense Council of Ukraine; You can familiarize yourself with the current sanctions list on the website of the Verkhovna Rada of Ukraine at the link: https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/n0004525-20#Text legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities or individuals who have violated the Law of Ukraine “On Ensuring the Rights and Freedoms of Citizens and the Legal Regime in the Temporarily Occupied Territory of Ukraine” dated 15.04.2014 № 1207-VII.

Technical requirements
The submitted applications must comply with the following technical requirements : The project is being implemented in cooperation between Ukrainian and international institution(s) or organisation(s) (museum, gallery, fair, festival, etc. in the country of the project implementation) that have the institutional capacity and experience in implementing similar projects and / or objects of intellectual property that can be used in the process of carrying out the exhibition project and organising the exhibition.  List of recommended partnership institutions abroad available here . The project is being implemented in one of the Ukrainian Institute’s target countries as of 2026 (The Republic of Poland, the Federal Republic of Germany, the French Republic, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, the Slovak Republic, the United States of America, the Kingdom of the Netherlands, the Republic of Lithuania, the Republic of South Africa, the Federative Republic of Brazil, the United Mexican States, the Argentine Republic, the Republic of India, the Republic of Indonesia,Hungary). The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to implement exhibition projects in other countries on a case-by-case basis. The project showcases Ukrainian photography and/or addresses the overarching themes of the Ukrainian Institute’s activities: Russia’s War Against Ukraine Ukraine’s Recovery and Future Civil Society as the Foundation of Statehood Crimea and the Crimean Tatars Decolonization of culture and reappropriation of cultural heritage Iconic figures, phenomena, and events The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to support the implementation of selected projects on other topics, depending on the circumstances The start of the project is scheduled no earlier than March 1, 2027. The application is submitted in due time. The application is submitted in accordance with the provided form in Ukrainian (and if necessary in English). All necessary supporting documentation in accordance with the requirements below has been summitted. Each section of the application is filled in without exceeding the number of characters specified in the application form.",Visualise – support for international exhibition projects with Ukrainian partners,"The following entities are eligible to apply: legal bodies of all forms of ownership and private entrepreneurs registered in Ukraine with a confirmed prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one; organisations and companies registered outside of Ukraine, their branch offices and delegations registered and certified in Ukraine with a confirmed institutional capacity and prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one.

Applications submitted by individuals, legal entities registered both in Ukraine and abroad, related to the aggressor state – the Russian Federation, which is recognized as such in accordance with the Law of Ukraine“ “On the Prohibition of Propaganda of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime, Armed Aggression of the Russian Federation as a Terrorist State against Ukraine, Symbolism of the Military Invasion of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime into Ukraine”№ 2265-ІХ of May 22, 2022, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran, are considered ineligible, namely: legal entities with beneficiaries who are individuals – citizens of the aggressor state of the Russian Federation, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran or or legal entities associated with the aggressor state of the Russian Federation and the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran; legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities to whom personal special economic and other restrictive measures (sanctions) have been applied in accordance with the Law of Ukraine “On Sanctions” and decisions of the National Security and Defense Council of Ukraine; You can familiarize yourself with the current sanctions list on the website of the Verkhovna Rada of Ukraine at the link: https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/n0004525-20#Text legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities or individuals who have violated the Law of Ukraine “On Ensuring the Rights and Freedoms of Citizens and the Legal Regime in the Temporarily Occupied Territory of Ukraine” dated 15.04.2014 № 1207-VII.

Technical requirements
The submitted applications must comply with the following technical requirements : The project is being implemented in cooperation between Ukrainian and international institution(s) or organisation(s) (museum, gallery, fair, festival, etc. in the country of the project implementation) that have the institutional capacity and experience in implementing similar projects and / or objects of intellectual property that can be used in the process of carrying out the exhibition project and organising the exhibition.  List of recommended partnership institutions abroad available here . The project is being implemented in one of the Ukrainian Institute’s target countries as of 2026 (The Republic of Poland, the Federal Republic of Germany, the French Republic, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, the Slovak Republic, the United States of America, the Kingdom of the Netherlands, the Republic of Lithuania, the Republic of South Africa, the Federative Republic of Brazil, the United Mexican States, the Argentine Republic, the Republic of India, the Republic of Indonesia,Hungary). The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to implement exhibition projects in other countries on a case-by-case basis. The project showcases Ukrainian photography and/or addresses the overarching themes of the Ukrainian Institute’s activities: Russia’s War Against Ukraine Ukraine’s Recovery and Future Civil Society as the Foundation of Statehood Crimea and the Crimean Tatars Decolonization of culture and reappropriation of cultural heritage Iconic figures, phenomena, and events The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to support the implementation of selected projects on other topics, depending on the circumstances The start of the project is scheduled no earlier than March 1, 2027. The application is submitted in due time. The application is submitted in accordance with the provided form in Ukrainian (and if necessary in English). All necessary supporting documentation in accordance with the requirements below has been summitted. Each section of the application is filled in without exceeding the number of characters specified in the application form.",01 Nov 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.038418+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d62c210c4b06,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/premiere-concours/,https://festivita.be/premierecompetition/,FestiVita!,"Dedicated to music performed on period instruments, cs by highlighting the uniqueness of their artistic, scholarly, and interpretive approaches. It is precisely this subtle balance of qualities that the event strives to reveal to an open and enthusiastic audience.",music,competition,Belgium,Brussels,"For this performance, each winning artist will receive a fee of minimum 500 EUR.",,new generation,en,“PREMIÈRE” CONCOURS,"The aim here is to highlight small ensembles of the new generation, capable of bringing the competition’s three objectives—artistic, scientific, and rhetorical—into dialogue with brilliance and originality.",“PREMIÈRE” CONCOURS,"The aim here is to highlight small ensembles of the new generation, capable of bringing the competition’s three objectives—artistic, scientific, and rhetorical—into dialogue with brilliance and originality.",01 Nov 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.042204+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2c25abbd7783,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/premiere-concours-2027/,https://festivita.be/premierecompetition/,FestiVita! Brussels Early Music Festival,"Festi Vita! is excited to announce the 5th edition of the Early Music Competition Première. This year’s theme is “Madrid and Spain” . The event will be held at the Cercle Royal Gaulois in Brussels on February 13, 2027. Check out the requirements and spread the word! The Première Early Music competition on historical instruments seeks to promote young musicians who bring their artistic, scholarly, and rhetorical approach to the fore. It is the subtle balance between all these qualities that the competition seeks to reveal to an open-minded and enthusiastic public. Early music is in a constant flux, and its performance codes keep evolving as performers explore and re-visit historical sources. This competition is an ideal opportunity to refresh early music, to offer it new purposes, and new vitality.",Early Music,competition,Belgium,Brussels,Price,,young musicians,en,Première Concours 2027,"The Première Early Music competition on historical instruments seeks to promote young musicians who bring their artistic, scholarly, and rhetorical approach to the fore.",Première Concours 2027,"The Première Early Music competition on historical instruments seeks to promote young musicians who bring their artistic, scholarly, and rhetorical approach to the fore.",01 Nov 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.045389+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_9c1b52c8ff2d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-teatri-riflessi-festival-2027-international-short-performance-competition/,https://www.iterculture.eu/en/teatri-riflessi/tr2027/tr12/,Teatri Riflessi Festival,"Teatri Riflessi Festival has opened its 2027 call for short performances: live works no longer than 15 minutes of contemporary dance, theatre, circus or multidisciplinary performance.","contemporary dance, theatre, circus or multidisciplinary performance",International Short Performance Competition,Italy,"Zafferana Etnea, Sicily","Selected works will receive a cachet ranging from €500 to €1,100 (based on the number of performers on stage) and partial support for travel expenses, compete in front of numerous Italian and international professionals (theatre and festival directors, dance networks coordinators, programmers, residency centres, critics and scholars) for several monetary prizes and the possibility of receiving touring and artist residency opportunities.",Free application,,en,Open Call Teatri Riflessi Festival 2027 – International Short Performance Competition,"live works no longer than 15 minutes of contemporary dance, theatre, circus or multidisciplinary performance.",Open Call Teatri Riflessi Festival 2027 – International Short Performance Competition,"live works no longer than 15 minutes of contemporary dance, theatre, circus or multidisciplinary performance.",15 October 2026 (17:00 CEST),2026-10-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.051715+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_81744cb359a1,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/support-for-international-showcasing-of-co-creation-projects/,https://zmina.eu/en/calls/zmina-resilience-showcasing,IZOLYATSIA Foundation (UA) and Malý Berlín (SK) together with Trans Europe Halles (SE),The objective of this call is to support projects that bring artistic and cultural works co-created by Ukrainian and other Creative Europe cultural organisations to wider audiences through public showcasing and presentation events in Ukraine and across other Creative Europe countries.,All creative and cultural sectors except audiovisual,rolling open call,Ukraine and other Creative Europe countries,,"Total funding available: 950,000 € Grant amount: up to 50,000 €, covering up to 90% of total project costs. The remaining 10% must be covered by the applicants as their own contribution in monetary form (not in-kind) and reflected in their accounting statements.",,,en,Support for International Showcasing of co-creation projects,"Funding will be provided to projects featuring co-creations made by partnerships involving at least one organisation from Ukraine and at least one organisation from another Creative Europe country. The projects should maximise the visibility, audience reach, sustainability, and future showcasing potential of these works. Supported projects are expected to include active partner cooperation to adapt showcased works to new audiences, for example by contextualising works, providing translation, involving local artists, experts and communities, conducting parallel programmes, and similar approaches. All creative and cultural sectors are eligible except audiovisual. Project Objectives Showcase and tour co-creations that explore the theme of resilience in any arts or cultural sector except audiovisual. Hold a minimum of 6 public presentation events: at least 3 events in each of at least two countries, one of which must be Ukraine. The presentation events cannot take place in the home city or town of any of the applicant organisations.",Support for International Showcasing of co-creation projects,"Funding will be provided to projects featuring co-creations made by partnerships involving at least one organisation from Ukraine and at least one organisation from another Creative Europe country. The projects should maximise the visibility, audience reach, sustainability, and future showcasing potential of these works. Supported projects are expected to include active partner cooperation to adapt showcased works to new audiences, for example by contextualising works, providing translation, involving local artists, experts and communities, conducting parallel programmes, and similar approaches. All creative and cultural sectors are eligible except audiovisual. Project Objectives Showcase and tour co-creations that explore the theme of resilience in any arts or cultural sector except audiovisual. Hold a minimum of 6 public presentation events: at least 3 events in each of at least two countries, one of which must be Ukraine. The presentation events cannot take place in the home city or town of any of the applicant organisations.",14 Oct 2026,2026-10-14,2026-09-23 12:37:25.054717+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_80e592b53200,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/speel-je-showcase-of-pitch-je-project-op-classicalnext-2027/,https://www.classicalnext.org/index.php,Classical:NEXT,The largest global gathering of professionals for all sectors of classical and art music,classical and art music,open call,Poland,Katowice,,,,en,Submit your programme proposal or showcase for Classical:NEXT,"Classical:NEXT 2027 is looking for bold ideas and trailblazing voices for their conference in Katowice, Poland from 11 to 14 May 2027. Whether it’s early or contemporary, traditional or experimental, live or recorded, educational, artistic or focusing on business, what matters is that it’s heading NEXT .",Submit your programme proposal or showcase for Classical:NEXT,"Classical:NEXT 2027 is looking for bold ideas and trailblazing voices for their conference in Katowice, Poland from 11 to 14 May 2027. Whether it’s early or contemporary, traditional or experimental, live or recorded, educational, artistic or focusing on business, what matters is that it’s heading NEXT .",09 Oct 2026,2026-10-09,2026-09-23 12:37:25.057613+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_ca6c04cf8273,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/theaterfestival-quartieri-di-vita-napels-zoekt-een-maker-regisseur/,,"Flanders Arts Institute, Flemish Diplomatic Representation in Rome",The ‘ Quartieri di Vita ’ theatre festival (Naples) is looking for a creator/director from Flanders to work with vulnerable groups from the Campania region for two weeks.,performing arts,festival,Italy,Naples,"A per diem of approximately €50.00 per day and an artistic fee of €1,300.00 for the two weeks will be provided.",,,en,‘Quartieri di Vita’ theatre festival (Naples) is looking for a creator/director,"You are active in, and connected to, the Flemish art scene; you have a socially engaged art practice and demonstrable experience of participatory work: working with vulnerable groups. You must be available for the entire period, from 19 to 29 November, on site (departure no later than 18 November and return no earlier than 30 November 2026). It is not essential to speak or understand Italian, but it is an advantage. You are affiliated with an arts organisation in Flanders that works in the field of participation, or you invite an arts organisation in Flanders to follow the process remotely, which has an interest in building relationships with socially engaged practices in the Naples region and in following up on the project after the workshop.",‘Quartieri di Vita’ theatre festival (Naples) is looking for a creator/director,"You are active in, and connected to, the Flemish art scene; you have a socially engaged art practice and demonstrable experience of participatory work: working with vulnerable groups. You must be available for the entire period, from 19 to 29 November, on site (departure no later than 18 November and return no earlier than 30 November 2026). It is not essential to speak or understand Italian, but it is an advantage. You are affiliated with an arts organisation in Flanders that works in the field of participation, or you invite an arts organisation in Flanders to follow the process remotely, which has an interest in building relationships with socially engaged practices in the Naples region and in following up on the project after the workshop.",Friday 2 October at 23:59,2026-10-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.063598+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_3511fb00ced1,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-voor-collectieven/,https://form.jotform.com/261593458605364,wpZimmer,"A technically-equipped studio space of approx. 18m x 17m A medium sized atelier space with limited technical equipment, also adapted to physical practices of approx. 4m x 13m Shared accommodation for max. 6 people per residency slot. A financial contribution of €5.000 excl. VAT per collective; we expect the budget to be managed by the collective. Beyond the workspace, accommodation and financial contribution, wpZimmer opens up its community as well as its knowledge. We value a reciprocal way of working between the artists and our team.",Your practice does not rely on one discipline or medium; it moves freely between contexts/themes;,Residency,Belgium,,A financial contribution of €5.000 excl. VAT per collective,,,en,Open call voor collectieven,"You are an already existing, new or temporary collective of artists/artworkers based in Belgium with the desire to further develop your collective practice. Your collective consists of min. 3 artists or art workers. You are looking for a space to experiment with collectivity and collective practices; You have a process-oriented approach; in other words, you are not focused on a single project, but rather an emerging practice and/or methodology; Your practice does not rely on one discipline or medium; it moves freely between contexts/themes; Your practice aims to bring people together in non-traditional or innovative ways; it is not based on the classic black box setting or white cube approach. You are interested in nurturing a reciprocal relationship with wpZimmer.",Open call voor collectieven,"You are an already existing, new or temporary collective of artists/artworkers based in Belgium with the desire to further develop your collective practice. Your collective consists of min. 3 artists or art workers. You are looking for a space to experiment with collectivity and collective practices; You have a process-oriented approach; in other words, you are not focused on a single project, but rather an emerging practice and/or methodology; Your practice does not rely on one discipline or medium; it moves freely between contexts/themes; Your practice aims to bring people together in non-traditional or innovative ways; it is not based on the classic black box setting or white cube approach. You are interested in nurturing a reciprocal relationship with wpZimmer.",20 Sep 2026,2026-09-20,2026-09-23 12:37:25.069633+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_8348a7d5baaf,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/residency-programme-2027/,https://institutotropical.com/page65686369.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com,Instituto Tropical,"Instituto Tropical invites artists and curators from all disciplines to apply with an ongoing artistic or curatorial research project for one of two residency periods in 2027. The programme offers a space to tropicalize that research through situated processes engaging the land, local communities, and ‘Ancestral Intelligences’ (AI). It offers time for exchange, experimentation, and collective inquiry — fostering encounters with ancient knowledge systems, local arts and craft techniques, scientific knowledge, and eco-social technologies of agriculture within already existing feeding systems. The programme offers a space and time to decolonize the senses, and to explore different economies of perception and attention.",artists and curators from all disciplines,residency programme,,,"The residency costs 900€ – which includes 10 to 12 days accommodation, meals, transport and meetings with experts. Two or three meetings with experts (as mentioned above) Transport to and from CDMX upon arrival/ departure of residency",,,en,Residency Programme 2027,Instituto Tropical invites artists and curators from all disciplines to apply with an ongoing artistic or curatorial research project for one of two residency periods in 2027. The open call residency programme for institutionally or state fund international artists and curators helps to fund the work with indigenous knowledge practitioners and the artistic residencies of first nations artists and curators.,Residency Programme 2027,Instituto Tropical invites artists and curators from all disciplines to apply with an ongoing artistic or curatorial research project for one of two residency periods in 2027. The open call residency programme for institutionally or state fund international artists and curators helps to fund the work with indigenous knowledge practitioners and the artistic residencies of first nations artists and curators.,15 Sep 2026,2026-09-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.074401+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_6e69a631d20d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-concepts-steiger-gallery/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdTCGtV5h0Izt9VY1QmrLbIz2Ic3UMYAcip0LuuWJ01W5_qZw/viewform,Steiger Gallery,"The Steiger Gallery is seeking artistic concepts for the Wassergarten at Erlebnisort Reden in Saarland, Germany.",all disciplines,open call,Germany,Saarland,"The total project budget, including artist‘s fee, production, and installation, should range between €2,000 and €60,000.",,emerging and established artists,en,Call for Concepts – Steiger Gallery,"To apply, emerging and established artists from all disciplines are invited to participate. Regional, national, and international submissions are expressly encouraged. The concepts must be feasible for the artists to implement independently. To protect the local wildlife, installations that produce loud bangs are excluded from the application process. Artworks containing racist, anti-Semitic, sexist, transphobic or ableist content, or which are otherwise inhumane or discriminatory, are excluded from participation. The concepts must be suitable for installation in a public outdoor space. In particular, weather conditions and the risk of vandalism must be taken into account when selecting materials and designing the construction.",Call for Concepts – Steiger Gallery,"To apply, emerging and established artists from all disciplines are invited to participate. Regional, national, and international submissions are expressly encouraged. The concepts must be feasible for the artists to implement independently. To protect the local wildlife, installations that produce loud bangs are excluded from the application process. Artworks containing racist, anti-Semitic, sexist, transphobic or ableist content, or which are otherwise inhumane or discriminatory, are excluded from participation. The concepts must be suitable for installation in a public outdoor space. In particular, weather conditions and the risk of vandalism must be taken into account when selecting materials and designing the construction.",13 Sep 2026,2026-09-13,2026-09-23 12:37:25.078813+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_16f5933a3038,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-project-pitch-session-transnational-ensemble-collaborations/,,field notes,"We invite ensembles, collectives, artists and curators to present projects at the Time to Listen conference that explore creative forms of transnational collaboration in the independent music scene.",independent music scene,project pitches,Germany,Berlin,A fee of €100 gross will be paid for the project presentation.,null,,en,Call: Project Pitch Session – Transnational Ensemble Collaborations,"We invite ensembles, collectives, artists and curators to present projects at the Time to Listen conference that explore creative forms of transnational collaboration in the independent music scene. We are looking for projects and approaches that go beyond conventional (international) co-production models and experiment with new ways of exchanging, producing together and sharing resources. These may include sustainable, solidarity-based or experimental forms of cooperation – between ensembles, within broader networks, or in constellations that deliberately question and rethink existing structures. Of particular interest are approaches that enable long-term collaboration, share knowledge and responsibility, and respond to current ecological, political and financial challenges. Projects at different stages of development are welcome, from initial ideas that are open to additional partners joining, to projects that have already been implemented – whether successfully or, equally welcome, unsuccessfully. We are interested in proposals that open up new perspectives on collaboration across borders and contexts. If you are interested, please send a short abstract (max. 1 page) outlining the project, along with brief information about yourself, by 4 September 2026 via email to info@field-notes.berlin .",Call: Project Pitch Session – Transnational Ensemble Collaborations,"We invite ensembles, collectives, artists and curators to present projects at the Time to Listen conference that explore creative forms of transnational collaboration in the independent music scene. We are looking for projects and approaches that go beyond conventional (international) co-production models and experiment with new ways of exchanging, producing together and sharing resources. These may include sustainable, solidarity-based or experimental forms of cooperation – between ensembles, within broader networks, or in constellations that deliberately question and rethink existing structures. Of particular interest are approaches that enable long-term collaboration, share knowledge and responsibility, and respond to current ecological, political and financial challenges. Projects at different stages of development are welcome, from initial ideas that are open to additional partners joining, to projects that have already been implemented – whether successfully or, equally welcome, unsuccessfully. We are interested in proposals that open up new perspectives on collaboration across borders and contexts. If you are interested, please send a short abstract (max. 1 page) outlining the project, along with brief information about yourself, by 4 September 2026 via email to info@field-notes.berlin .",4 September 2026,2026-09-04,2026-09-23 12:37:25.084506+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2a53d6b47ce2,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/pairing-is-caring-2026-2027-op-zoek-naar-mentors/,https://framaforms.org/paring-is-caring-2026-1778770204,"Flanders Arts Institute, The Gap, NICC","It can be particularly difficult for emerging artists to find their way in the professional field. Through Pairing is Caring , we pair an emerging artist with a more experienced artist or cultural professional (a ‘mentor’), so that knowledge about building an artistic career can be shared.","performing arts, performance art, the visual arts, digital arts and multimedia",Call,,Brussels,,,emerging artists,en,Wanted: Mentors who would like to support emerging artists,This call for applications is aimed exclusively at mentors.,Wanted: Mentors who would like to support emerging artists,This call for applications is aimed exclusively at mentors.,01 Sep 2026,2026-09-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.088898+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_32cfae041bea,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/lichtkunstwerk-voor-het-stadhuis-van-leuven/,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/lichtkunstwerk-voor-het-stadhuis-van-leuven/,"City of Leuven, LOV2030, Shift","The City of Leuven, LOV2030 and Shift are looking for an artist (or artist collective) for a new, temporary light artwork on the scaffolding canvas of Leuven’s historic town hall, to be presented during Wintertijd.",light artwork,Commission,Belgium,Leuven,"A budget of € 50,000 is available for this commission, including VAT and production costs.",,,en,Light artwork for Leuven Town Hall,"We are looking for a light sculpture that is aesthetically and conceptually strong, while also being visually appealing and accessible to a broad audience.",Light artwork for Leuven Town Hall,"We are looking for a light sculpture that is aesthetically and conceptually strong, while also being visually appealing and accessible to a broad audience.",1 September 2026,2026-09-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.093855+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_027f9c38db13,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/residency-open-call-2027/,https://arteventura.eu/artists-in-residence/open-call,Arteventura Residency,Arteventura welcomes professional artists from all contemporary disciplines to apply.,all contemporary disciplines,residency,Spain,Corteconcepción (Huelva),This call is for a paid residency.,You do not have to pay the (20 euro) application fee.,professional artists,en,Residency Open Call 2027,"The application is open for all professional artists. Artists can apply individual, as a duo or in group. If you are applying as a duo, both artists have to fill in the application and have to mention the name of their partner. Groups are welcome up to 10 people. • Arteventura offers silence, space and time to engage in research and development. • To get an idea of your personal work we ask to send in a portfolio and a brief description of your artistic practice or research. • Add a motivation letter explaining why you want to stay at arteventura, what you expect from the residency and what you would like to achieve. • Arteventura is a sustainable (of-the-grid) project. We ask the artists to consider this and share our vision. Tell us in a few words how you support this vision. • We encourage artists to share the research or its results at the end of the residency. • We are very pleased when an artist leaves a work, however this is not mandatory. These works will enter the arteventura collection and will be shared with a wider audience. • Arteventura doesn’t receive any financial support. Running a residency has overhead costs and daily running costs. The residency fee contributes to pay a part of these costs. • We encourage selected artists to apply for grants and will provide invitation letters and other relevant information needed.",Residency Open Call 2027,"The application is open for all professional artists. Artists can apply individual, as a duo or in group. If you are applying as a duo, both artists have to fill in the application and have to mention the name of their partner. Groups are welcome up to 10 people. • Arteventura offers silence, space and time to engage in research and development. • To get an idea of your personal work we ask to send in a portfolio and a brief description of your artistic practice or research. • Add a motivation letter explaining why you want to stay at arteventura, what you expect from the residency and what you would like to achieve. • Arteventura is a sustainable (of-the-grid) project. We ask the artists to consider this and share our vision. Tell us in a few words how you support this vision. • We encourage artists to share the research or its results at the end of the residency. • We are very pleased when an artist leaves a work, however this is not mandatory. These works will enter the arteventura collection and will be shared with a wider audience. • Arteventura doesn’t receive any financial support. Running a residency has overhead costs and daily running costs. The residency fee contributes to pay a part of these costs. • We encourage selected artists to apply for grants and will provide invitation letters and other relevant information needed.",30 Aug 2026,2026-08-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.096890+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_c218753995d0,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/nutrimenti_habitat-creativo-2026-tangible-practices-for-being-together/,https://www.associazionedemetra.it/nutrimenti_habitat-creativo-2026/,associazione demetra,Nutrimenti_Habitat Creativo 2026 – “Tangible Practices for Being Together”,"performance, participatory practices, site-specific and community-based projects in urban space",Residency,Italy,Terni,€1000 (gross) artist fee per artist/collective €350 food allowance travel reimbursement logistical and organisational support,,,en,Nutrimenti_Habitat Creativo 2026 – “Tangible Practices for Being Together”,"Participants: up to 3 artists and/or collectives, national and international Scope: performance, participatory practices, site-specific and community-based projects in urban space Conditions: shared accommodation and coworking space",Nutrimenti_Habitat Creativo 2026 – “Tangible Practices for Being Together”,"Participants: up to 3 artists and/or collectives, national and international Scope: performance, participatory practices, site-specific and community-based projects in urban space Conditions: shared accommodation and coworking space",15 Aug 2026,2026-08-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.100239+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_022c12b266e3,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-carroussa-sonore/,http://forms.gle/Ndt74iNqRyiWJ1cN8,Kunsten,"ARTISTS ARE INVITED TO SUBMIT SOUND WORKS FOR THE OPPORTUNITY TO BE FEATURED IN A CURATED COLLECTIVE SOUND ART PERFORMANCE IN PUBLIC SPACE THROUGH THE SPEAKERS OF CARROUSSA SONORE, A PROJECT BY ARTIST YOUNES BABA-ALI.",sound art,open call,Belgium,Antwerp,A PARTICIPATION HONORARIUM OF €185 (EX.VAT) IS PROVIDED PER PARTICIPATING ARTIST AS PART OF THIS PROJECT.,null,null,en,OPEN CALL CARROUSSA SONORE,"THIS CALL FOR PARTICIPATION IS OPEN TO ANY ARTIST, ASSOCIATION, OR COLLECTIVE OF INTERNATIONAL ARTISTS WITHOUT AGE LIMIT. A PARTICIPATION HONORARIUM OF €185 (EX.VAT) IS PROVIDED PER PARTICIPATING ARTIST AS PART OF THIS PROJECT. CANDIDATES CAN APPLY BY FILLING IN THIS GOOGLE FORM . IMPORTANT NOTE: IN ORDER TO BEABLE TO MAKE THE PAYMENT OF THE FEE WHEN SELECTED, ARTISTS MUSTBEABLE TO INVOICE (EITHER THROUGH THEIR OWN STRUCTURE ORATHIRD PARTY).",OPEN CALL CARROUSSA SONORE,"THIS CALL FOR PARTICIPATION IS OPEN TO ANY ARTIST, ASSOCIATION, OR COLLECTIVE OF INTERNATIONAL ARTISTS WITHOUT AGE LIMIT. A PARTICIPATION HONORARIUM OF €185 (EX.VAT) IS PROVIDED PER PARTICIPATING ARTIST AS PART OF THIS PROJECT. CANDIDATES CAN APPLY BY FILLING IN THIS GOOGLE FORM . IMPORTANT NOTE: IN ORDER TO BEABLE TO MAKE THE PAYMENT OF THE FEE WHEN SELECTED, ARTISTS MUSTBEABLE TO INVOICE (EITHER THROUGH THEIR OWN STRUCTURE ORATHIRD PARTY).",15 Aug 2026,2026-08-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.103163+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_c491dbaacb88,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-2026-finno-ugric-creative-residency-in-narva/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScQMVMcM-I2XeQitlnQq3frY4MTg8ceVSAeREZ1rIu8Qf_0DA/viewform,Narva Art Residency,"Narva Art Residency announces an open call for a Finno-Ugric creative residency, which will take place in late 2026.","visual art, music, theatre, and performance",Residency,Estonia,Narva,"We offer the artist an Erasmus+ per diem allowance, which is 170€ per day (1700€ for the period of the residency, 10 days). The accommodation is provided at NART building for the rate of 45€ per day (450€ for the period of the residency). The Erasmus+ support also covers any costs that go towards the production of the artwork. The reimbursement of the travel costs is provided separately and in addition to the per diems, following the guidelines of the Erasmus+ programme.",,,en,2026 FINNO-UGRIC CREATIVE RESIDENCY IN NARVA,"We are looking for applications from artists and creative people with roots from or strong ties to the Finno-Ugric peoples. The call is open to various creative fields, including visual art, music, theatre, and performance. The residency comes with support from the Erasmus+ programme and is therefore directed to applicants from eligible countries (see the list here ). In 2026, the second edition of the programme will include new features. As before, the selected artist is expected to create a work inspired by Finno-Ugric cultures. Additionally, they will collaborate closely with the Department of Fashion Design of the Estonian Academy of Arts. The collaboration will consist of an open lecture for the academy’s students (1,5h) and two workshops for the fashion design students (5h and 1,5h). From the artist-in-residence we expect a unique contemporary art project that introduces Finno-Ugric culture in a new and engaging form; a willingness to involve the local Narva community and introduce and present their work; engage with the students of EKA and give them a workshop and an open lecture which are connected to the topics of Finno-Ugric cultures, as well as participation in the residency during the period from November 23rd until December 6th. The application should be filled out in English.",2026 FINNO-UGRIC CREATIVE RESIDENCY IN NARVA,"We are looking for applications from artists and creative people with roots from or strong ties to the Finno-Ugric peoples. The call is open to various creative fields, including visual art, music, theatre, and performance. The residency comes with support from the Erasmus+ programme and is therefore directed to applicants from eligible countries (see the list here ). In 2026, the second edition of the programme will include new features. As before, the selected artist is expected to create a work inspired by Finno-Ugric cultures. Additionally, they will collaborate closely with the Department of Fashion Design of the Estonian Academy of Arts. The collaboration will consist of an open lecture for the academy’s students (1,5h) and two workshops for the fashion design students (5h and 1,5h). From the artist-in-residence we expect a unique contemporary art project that introduces Finno-Ugric culture in a new and engaging form; a willingness to involve the local Narva community and introduce and present their work; engage with the students of EKA and give them a workshop and an open lecture which are connected to the topics of Finno-Ugric cultures, as well as participation in the residency during the period from November 23rd until December 6th. The application should be filled out in English.",10 Aug 2026,2026-08-10,2026-09-23 12:37:25.106105+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_98e9614f22f8,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-submission-finno-ugric-creative-residency-in-narva-estonia/,https://www.nart.ee/en/open-call-2026-finno-ugric-creative-residency-in-narva/,Narva Art Residency,"Narva Art Residency announces an open call for a Finno-Ugric creative residency, which will take place in late 2026.","visual art, music, theatre, and performance",residency,Estonia,Narva,"We offer the artist an Erasmus+ per diem allowance, which is 170€ per day (1700€ for the period of the residency, 10 days). This is to cover the accommodation at NART, daily costs and other costs related to the residency. The accommodation is provided at NART building for the rate of 45€ per day (450€ for the period of the residency). The Erasmus+ support also covers any costs that go towards the production of the artwork. The reimbursement of the travel costs is provided separately and in addition to the per diems, following the guidelines of the Erasmus+ programme. The amount depends on the distance between the place of domicile and Narva, Estonia.",,,en,Open Call Submission: Finno-Ugric Creative Residency In Narva (Estonia),"We are looking for applications from artists and creative people with roots from or strong ties to the Finno-Ugric peoples. The call is open to various creative fields, including visual art, music, theatre, and performance. The residency comes with support from the Erasmus+ programme and is therefore directed to applicants from eligible countries (see the list here ). In 2026, the second edition of the programme will include new features. As before, the selected artist is expected to create a work inspired by Finno-Ugric cultures. Additionally, they will collaborate closely with the Department of Fashion Design of the Estonian Academy of Arts. The collaboration will consist of an open lecture for the academy’s students (1,5h) and two workshops for the fashion design students (5h and 1,5h). From the artist-in-residence we expect a unique contemporary art project that introduces Finno-Ugric culture in a new and engaging form; a willingness to involve the local Narva community and introduce and present their work; engage with the students of EKA and give them a workshop and an open lecture which are connected to the topics of Finno-Ugric cultures, as well as participation in the residency during the period from November 23rd until December 6th.",Open Call Submission: Finno-Ugric Creative Residency In Narva (Estonia),"We are looking for applications from artists and creative people with roots from or strong ties to the Finno-Ugric peoples. The call is open to various creative fields, including visual art, music, theatre, and performance. The residency comes with support from the Erasmus+ programme and is therefore directed to applicants from eligible countries (see the list here ). In 2026, the second edition of the programme will include new features. As before, the selected artist is expected to create a work inspired by Finno-Ugric cultures. Additionally, they will collaborate closely with the Department of Fashion Design of the Estonian Academy of Arts. The collaboration will consist of an open lecture for the academy’s students (1,5h) and two workshops for the fashion design students (5h and 1,5h). From the artist-in-residence we expect a unique contemporary art project that introduces Finno-Ugric culture in a new and engaging form; a willingness to involve the local Narva community and introduce and present their work; engage with the students of EKA and give them a workshop and an open lecture which are connected to the topics of Finno-Ugric cultures, as well as participation in the residency during the period from November 23rd until December 6th.",10 Aug 2026,2026-08-10,2026-09-23 12:37:25.109141+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_77d04eb32770,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-broedfestival-2027/,https://broedfestival.be/3/,Festival Stout vzw,"Have you been working on something for a while and would like to showcase your work at BROEDfestival? Great! Use this form to register for the 2027 Open Call, which gives you the opportunity to participate in BROEDfestival on February 22 and/or 23. BROEDfestival offers performing artists the chance to perform on one of our two festival days. Visual artists and multimedia creators can exhibit their work continuously in the hallways and spaces of c o r s o. If you showcase your work at BROED, you’ll be compensated for it and can access limited funding to further develop your work.",performing artists; visual artists; multimedia creators,open call; festival,,,you’ll be compensated for it and can access limited funding to further develop your work,,artists who haven’t yet had the chance to fully break into the professional sector,en,Open Call BROEDfestival 2027,"Because BROEDfestival aims primarily to support artists who haven’t yet had the chance to fully break into the professional sector, you and your project must meet the following requirements to submit an application: You are over 18 years of age. You have not received any major or structured grants or scholarships for the project you wish to submit. You do not yet have a (co-)producer for your project, nor an organization under whose wing you can create. Your artistic career is still in its relative infancy.",Open Call BROEDfestival 2027,"Because BROEDfestival aims primarily to support artists who haven’t yet had the chance to fully break into the professional sector, you and your project must meet the following requirements to submit an application: You are over 18 years of age. You have not received any major or structured grants or scholarships for the project you wish to submit. You do not yet have a (co-)producer for your project, nor an organization under whose wing you can create. Your artistic career is still in its relative infancy.",01 Aug 2026,2026-08-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.112199+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_5a5e4ce2e090,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/gezocht-opkomende-kunstenaars-die-op-zoek-zijn-naar-begeleiding/,https://framaforms.org/pairing-is-caring-2026-application-1781945486,"Kunstenpunt, The Gap, NICC","It can be particularly difficult for emerging artists to find their way in the professional field. Through Pairing is Caring , we pair an emerging artist with a more experienced artist or cultural professional (a ‘mentor’), so that knowledge about building an artistic career can be shared.","performing arts, performance art, visual arts, digital arts and multimedia",Call,Belgium,Brussels,,,emerging artists,en,Wanted: Emerging artists looking for guidance in the arts field,"Artists We focus on the performing arts, performance art, the visual arts, digital arts and multimedia .",Wanted: Emerging artists looking for guidance in the arts field,"Artists We focus on the performing arts, performance art, the visual arts, digital arts and multimedia .",30 Jul 2026,2026-07-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.115828+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_217b1f327dad,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ma-hoe-werkt-het-eigenlijk/,https://wp.assets.sh/uploads/sites/4718/2026/04/MAhoe_engels.pdf,MA Festival,During MA Festival 2026 you get the chance to talk to musicians and experts about what’s on your mind. You will also get a look behind the scenes by joining the volunteer crew for a few days.,performing music,Training,Belgium,Bruges,"Catering: we will provide meals for you from Tuesday 29/07 until Sunday evening 03/08. Accommodation: you will be accommodated free of charge in Bruges at boarding school Palaestra (check-in Monday 27/07 – check-out Monday 03/08). For the time you volunteer, you will receive an expense allowance of €11 per 4-hour shift You will receive a ticket for the opening concert of MA Festival on 01/08",,master’s degree or have just graduated,en,MA hoe werkt het eigenlijk? (‘But how does it work?’),"You are a performing musician
You are pursuing a master’s degree or have just graduated as a musician
