kunsten_be_flanders_edb8c38ba1df,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/visio-european-programme-on-artists-moving-images/,https://www.schermodellarte.org/en/visio-2026/,Lo schermo dell’arte,"Lo schermo dell’arte presents the fifteenth edition of the VISIO – European Programme on Artists’ Moving Images, a research, residency, and production programme dedicated to young, Europe-based artists who use moving images in their artistic practice.",artists’ moving images,"research, residency, and production programme",Italy,Florence,"VISIO includes the VISIO Production Fund , a €35,000 production fund conceived in partnership with Centro per l’Arte Contemporanea Luigi Pecci (Prato), Fondazione In Between Art Film (Rome), MACBA Museu d’Art Contemporani de Barcelona (Barcelona), and with the support of Human Company , a historic enterprise and reference point in Italy for open-air hospitality, which also provides a reimbursement of participating artists’ travel expenses.",,young,en,VISIO – European Programme on Artists’ Moving Images,"dedicated to young, Europe-based artists who use moving images in their artistic practice. The 8 participants will be young European-based artists who work with moving images; they will be selected through an open call promoted in collaboration with some of Europe’s leading art academies and artist residencies.",VISIO – European Programme on Artists’ Moving Images,"dedicated to young, Europe-based artists who use moving images in their artistic practice. The 8 participants will be young European-based artists who work with moving images; they will be selected through an open call promoted in collaboration with some of Europe’s leading art academies and artist residencies.","Friday, May 15th, 2026",2026-05-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.221801+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2a9138c53cf6,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/nair-urban-space-installation-residency/,https://www.nart.ee/en/open-call-nair-2026/,Narva Art Residency (NART),"The NAIR urban space installation residency in Narva is back. In 2026, we will create a light installation on the edge of the city, in the Pähklimäe neighbourhood.","visual, spatial, and interdisciplinary fields",Residency,Estonia,Narva,"Stipend: €3,000 Production budget for the installation: €11,000 Travel costs for the artist are reimbursed up to €1,000",,,en,NAIR urban space installation residency,"We are inviting artists, architects, designers, and other creative practitioners from Estonia and abroad, working in both individual and collaborative practices across visual, spatial, and interdisciplinary fields, to apply. Applicants are required to submit a project proposal for a spatial installation or sculpture.",NAIR urban space installation residency,"We are inviting artists, architects, designers, and other creative practitioners from Estonia and abroad, working in both individual and collaborative practices across visual, spatial, and interdisciplinary fields, to apply. Applicants are required to submit a project proposal for a spatial installation or sculpture.",15 May 2026,2026-05-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.224663+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_45954c0f1127,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-full-contact-2026/,http://www.scan.cat/,SCAN Tarragona,"Full Contact is a professional meeting space aimed at photographers and visual creators working with photography who wish to present their projects to international experts . It offers a valuable opportunity to receive feedback, expand professional networks, and explore new opportunities within the contemporary photography scene.","photography, visual creators",open call,any European Union country or the United Kingdom,null,"A solo exhibition in 2027 as part of the official SCAN programme A fee of €900 (taxes included) for exhibition and communication rights Curatorial advice and support from the SCAN team, according to the festival’s technical and financial resources",,emerging artists,en,Open call for Full Contact 2026,"Eligibility: Persons of legal age residing in any European Union country or the United Kingdom Project type: The festival aims to promote visual storytelling among emerging artists. Any photographic series that tells a story may be submitted, regardless of subject",Open call for Full Contact 2026,"Eligibility: Persons of legal age residing in any European Union country or the United Kingdom Project type: The festival aims to promote visual storytelling among emerging artists. Any photographic series that tells a story may be submitted, regardless of subject",10 May 2026,2026-05-10,2026-09-23 12:37:25.228003+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0607d3ccd703,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/e10000-transitional-justice-grant-fellowship/,https://afield.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=793163623749ff92bce4091cd&id=8944611f3e&e=787e6c9df5,"AFIELD, Arts of the Working Class, and Framer Framed","Within a context marked by nationalism, climate displacement, and systemic discrimination, AFIELD, Arts of the Working Class, and Framer Framed invite artists, cultural practitioners, and collectives working with communities affected by human rights violations to apply for a €10,000 grant and a six-month fellowship . The Transitional Justice with Artists (TJA) program supports six Europe-based artists or practitioners with initiatives that engage deeply with truth, memory, repair, and accountability, to imagine justice beyond legal frameworks.",artists and cultural practitioners,grant and a six-month fellowship,EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country,Amsterdam,"€10,000 per fellow (€9,000 unrestricted funding + €1,000 for travel).",,,en,"€10,000 Transitional Justice Grant & Fellowship","Applicants must be: Legal residents (including refugees/asylum seekers) in an EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country . Part of an initiative operationally active for at least two years . Using artistic methodologies as the central component of their work. Available for all fellowship components , including the residency and online thematic meetings.","€10,000 Transitional Justice Grant & Fellowship","Applicants must be: Legal residents (including refugees/asylum seekers) in an EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country . Part of an initiative operationally active for at least two years . Using artistic methodologies as the central component of their work. Available for all fellowship components , including the residency and online thematic meetings.",02 May 2026,2026-05-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.231021+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_bf616e30e784,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/2026-visureal%c2%b7international-image-art-festival-viiaf-call-for-artists-and-art-organizations-worldwide/,https://viiaf.com/call-for-submissions/,VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF),The 2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF) invites submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide.,image-based art,Festival,China,Chengdu,,,,en,2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF): Call for Artists and Art Organizations Worldwide,submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide,2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF): Call for Artists and Art Organizations Worldwide,submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide,01 May 2026,2026-05-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.233634+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_e9cea19ce978,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-individual-mobility-2025-2026/,https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-for-individual-mobility-2025-2026,Culture Moves Europe,The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.,"architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts",Open call,,,"Daily allowance 85€ per day of project implementation. Travel allowance travel distance under 5 000 km -> 400€ travel distance from 5 000 km -> 800€ The travel distance is calculated automatically in the application form, based on a one-way straight line. The grant offers additional funding, if applicable: Top-ups Green mobility top-up: 400€ Overseas countries and territories / Outermost regions top-up: 175€ Family top-up: 200€ per child Visa top-up: 120€ Accessibility support 30€ per day of project implementation Either the actual cost or a fixed allowance for personal assistance or sign language interpretation, depending on the assistant’s professional status",,,en,Call for individual mobility 2025-2026,"Artists and cultural professionals, who are: legally residing in one of the Creative Europe countries, including the overseas countries and territories and outermost regions 18 years of age or older active in one of the following sectors: architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts; No specific level of experience is required The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.",Call for individual mobility 2025-2026,"Artists and cultural professionals, who are: legally residing in one of the Creative Europe countries, including the overseas countries and territories and outermost regions 18 years of age or older active in one of the following sectors: architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts; No specific level of experience is required The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.",30 Apr 2026,2026-04-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.236940+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_4aedc4760cc0,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-zoop-connections-ii-kunstfort-vijfhuizen-czech-centre-brussels-call-for-artist-in-residence-2026/,https://www.kunstfort.nl/en/news/open-call-kunstfort-vijfhuizen-x-czech-centre-brussels/,"Czech Centre Brussels, Kunstfort Vijfhuizen, EUNIC Netherlands, Zoöp, and DutchCulture","This residency and open call have been developed in collaboration with the Czech Centre Brussels, Kunstfort Vijfhuizen, EUNIC Netherlands, Zoöp, and DutchCulture, and are intended for artists, researchers, and creative practitioners with a connection to the Czech Republic or Czech cultural practice.","visual arts, design, research, literature, performance, music, technology, or other interdisciplinary practices",Residency,Netherlands,Vijfhuizen,"On-site accommodation
Daily stipend of €50
Travel expenses covered
Access to a workshop with tools and technical support",,,en,Open Call Zoöp Connections II: Kunstfort Vijfhuizen & Czech Centre Brussels Call for Artist-in-Residence 2026,"Creative professionals and artists aged 18+, based in a Creative Europe country outside the Netherlands, with a demonstrable connection to Czech culture. Residents may come from a wide range of creative fields, including visual arts, design, research, literature, performance, music, technology, or other interdisciplinary practices.",Open Call Zoöp Connections II: Kunstfort Vijfhuizen & Czech Centre Brussels Call for Artist-in-Residence 2026,"Creative professionals and artists aged 18+, based in a Creative Europe country outside the Netherlands, with a demonstrable connection to Czech culture. Residents may come from a wide range of creative fields, including visual arts, design, research, literature, performance, music, technology, or other interdisciplinary practices.",30 Apr 2026,2026-04-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.240403+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_b2bef0511012,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-residencies/,https://www.imal.org/en/events/appel-a-residences-ipo-2026-extra,iMAL,"iMAL Project Office is our yearly open call for residencies, aimed at artists based in Belgium. We announced our first three iPO 2026 calls last October. Now we can finally reveal the fourth, dedicated to a two-month co-creation residency in collaboration with Antre Peaux (Bourges, FR), and taking place in the framework of EXTRA RESIDENCIES.","visual arts, digital art and experimental video games",residency,Belgium,Brussels,,,emerging artists,en,Open call for residencies,"The call is open to emerging artists engaged in a professional practice. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works. Candidates must reside in France or Belgium.

Option 1: Duos to be formed
• Artists apply individually to the call without having a predefined partner. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates, then shared via Google Drive with all candidates on May 4.
• This stage will allow artists to review applications and connect with other candidates to explore the possibility of collaborating on a joint project. Candidates will have from May 4 to May 22 to engage in these exchanges.
• The pairs formed will be invited to complete a second questionnaire by May 22, with the name of their partner and a letter of intent regarding their co-creation project.

Option 2: Existing duos
• It is possible to apply directly with another artist for a co-creation project. The only prerequisite is that one artist must reside in France and the other in Belgium. Both artists are invited to respond individually to the call for applications, specifying that they are working on a joint project and providing the name of the artist they’re partnering with.
• Please note: Existing duos should only answer the first application form, which closes on April 24. They must therefore submit their letter of intent detailing their joint project using this form. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates.",Open call for residencies,"The call is open to emerging artists engaged in a professional practice. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works. Candidates must reside in France or Belgium.

Option 1: Duos to be formed
• Artists apply individually to the call without having a predefined partner. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates, then shared via Google Drive with all candidates on May 4.
• This stage will allow artists to review applications and connect with other candidates to explore the possibility of collaborating on a joint project. Candidates will have from May 4 to May 22 to engage in these exchanges.
• The pairs formed will be invited to complete a second questionnaire by May 22, with the name of their partner and a letter of intent regarding their co-creation project.

Option 2: Existing duos
• It is possible to apply directly with another artist for a co-creation project. The only prerequisite is that one artist must reside in France and the other in Belgium. Both artists are invited to respond individually to the call for applications, specifying that they are working on a joint project and providing the name of the artist they’re partnering with.
• Please note: Existing duos should only answer the first application form, which closes on April 24. They must therefore submit their letter of intent detailing their joint project using this form. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates.",24 Apr 2026,2026-04-24,2026-09-23 12:37:25.243981+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a97a4eca3212,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-international-fikva-award-for-painters-2026/,https://fikva.art/submission-form/,FiKVA Foundation,"The FiKVA Foundation proudly presents the 4th International FiKVA Award for Representational & Figurative Painters – a remarkable opportunity for artists worldwide to gain international recognition, share their talent globally, and earn substantial financial rewards. Best of all, the entire process is online – no need to ship your work or part with it!",painters / representational & figurative painting,award,,,"First Prize: €3500 cash prize + Art supplies package, courtesy of M. Graham (12 color paints, valued at €300) + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300 + Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of finalists + Published interview with the FiKVA Foundation + Permanent display of the submitted artwork on the FiKVA website + 6-month online gallery representation for a selected artwork; Second Prize: €1500 cash prize + Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of finalists + Published interview with the FiKVA Foundation + Permanent display of the submitted artwork on the FiKVA website + 6-month online gallery representation for a selected artwork + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Third Prize: €500 cash prize + Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of finalists + Published interview with the FiKVA Foundation + Permanent display of the submitted artwork on the FiKVA website + 6-month online gallery representation for a selected artwork + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Purchase Prize (only awarded if a work fits the objectives and possibilities of the FiKVa-collection): Acquisition of one selected artwork for the FiKVA Collection + Certificate of Achievement + Permanent display of the purchased artwork on the FiKVA website + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Honorable Mention (3 will be awarded): Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of the finalists + Permanent place on the FiKVA website + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Top 35: Participation in the online group exhibition of the finalists + Permanent display on the FiKVA website + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €200; Gallery Representation Prize: Up to 10 outstanding artworks from the Top 100 will be handpicked for a 6-month gallery representation with the FiKVA Online Gallery. This exclusive opportunity is by invitation only, with no obligation to the artist.",Participation in the FiKVA Award with just one work: €36,,en,OPEN CALL – International FIKVA Award for painters 2026,"The FiKVA Award is open to all artists 18 years of age or older.

ARTIST ELIGIBILITY
The FiKVA Award is open to all painters aged 18 and older, from anywhere in the world.

ARTWORK ELIGIBILITY
The work must be the artist’s original creation, produced solely by the artist, with copyrights exclusively owned by the artist. The work may be signed and may have participated in previous competitions. The work may be sold, provided the copyright of its image remains solely with the artist. Works must have been produced between 2024 and 2026. Works must be available for inclusion in an online exhibition. Works do not need to be available for sale.

ACCEPTED MEDIA
Oil, water-soluble oil paint, acrylic paint, watercolor, ink, gouache, tempera, and all traditional wet mediums on any support – canvas, board, paper, wood, panel, wall, aluminium, glass, etc. All works must be handmade; digital or mechanical works will not be considered.

SUBJECT MATTER & SIZE
No restrictions – submit what you consider your best work from the last two years.

HOW TO PARTICIPATE?
Registration is only possible via the website: www.fikva.art",OPEN CALL – International FIKVA Award for painters 2026,"The FiKVA Award is open to all artists 18 years of age or older.

ARTIST ELIGIBILITY
The FiKVA Award is open to all painters aged 18 and older, from anywhere in the world.

ARTWORK ELIGIBILITY
The work must be the artist’s original creation, produced solely by the artist, with copyrights exclusively owned by the artist. The work may be signed and may have participated in previous competitions. The work may be sold, provided the copyright of its image remains solely with the artist. Works must have been produced between 2024 and 2026. Works must be available for inclusion in an online exhibition. Works do not need to be available for sale.

ACCEPTED MEDIA
Oil, water-soluble oil paint, acrylic paint, watercolor, ink, gouache, tempera, and all traditional wet mediums on any support – canvas, board, paper, wood, panel, wall, aluminium, glass, etc. All works must be handmade; digital or mechanical works will not be considered.

SUBJECT MATTER & SIZE
No restrictions – submit what you consider your best work from the last two years.

HOW TO PARTICIPATE?
Registration is only possible via the website: www.fikva.art",22 Apr 2026,2026-04-22,2026-09-23 12:37:25.247182+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_5d9b2594f95d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/fellowship-programma-call-2026/,https://framaforms.org/imal-fellowship-programme-2026-1770642755,"iMAL, Cloud Seven","In a cultural landscape seeking new connections, the Fellowship Programme proposes a renewed alliance between artists and those who support the emergence of their work. A new cultural model based on an expanded mecenat: more open, more engaged, and more attentive to the shifts in the creative world.",contemporary art,production residency,Belgium,Brussels,"The artist will receive accommodation, a workspace, and a budget of €8,000 taxes included (€4,000 in fees and €4,000 for production).",,professional artists,en,Fellowship programme: call 2026,"This programme is specifically designed for professional artists who wish to shift or deepen their practice through technology. We are looking for candidates who: Have a solid background in contemporary art but limited experience with digital tools. Artists that while rooted in contemporary art, demonstrate an initial exploration of technological tools and show a strong interest in deepening this approach through a committed project requiring curatorial and technical support within iMAL. View this residency as a learning opportunity rather than a standard production slot. Are seeking curatorial mentorship and technical guidance to explore new territories. Note: Artists with extensive experience in digital arts may be considered overqualified, as the programme’s primary goal is to provide a space for growth, experimentation, and the acquisition of new technical and critical skills.",Fellowship programme: call 2026,"This programme is specifically designed for professional artists who wish to shift or deepen their practice through technology. We are looking for candidates who: Have a solid background in contemporary art but limited experience with digital tools. Artists that while rooted in contemporary art, demonstrate an initial exploration of technological tools and show a strong interest in deepening this approach through a committed project requiring curatorial and technical support within iMAL. View this residency as a learning opportunity rather than a standard production slot. Are seeking curatorial mentorship and technical guidance to explore new territories. Note: Artists with extensive experience in digital arts may be considered overqualified, as the programme’s primary goal is to provide a space for growth, experimentation, and the acquisition of new technical and critical skills.","Application Deadline: April 19, 2026",2026-04-19,2026-09-23 12:37:25.250072+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2fa2a89c4a72,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-raive-ai-summer-school/,https://raive.school/,The Algorithmic Gaze and CREATIE,"The Algorithmic Gaze and CREATIE, both Antwerp-based research groups, will join forces again to organise a summerschool for everyone who’s interested in the topic of performative AI and interdisciplinary creation. After two great editions, RAIVE will take place again between the 31st of August and the 6th of September in the Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp. RAIVE is a laboratory for young artists from diverse disciplines such as dance, music, technology, and visual arts. Artists come together to redefine the boundaries of their craft through the lens of interdisciplinary collaboration. Participants learn to create their own AI systems from basic principles, curating their own datasets through a very “hands-on” artistic approach. As participants, you will be divided into groups in which you will work for one week. During this process you both learn from each other and benefit from the insights of three coaches, skilled in different areas within the arts. The culmination of this week-long journey is a public presentation held in De Gele Zaal of the Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp.","dance, music, technology, and visual arts",summer school,Belgium,Antwerp,"The total price of the summer school is € 300,00 . Included in this price are: lunch, workshops, coachings, working space and technical equipment.","The total price of the summer school is € 300,00 .",young/starting artist,en,Open call – RAIVE AI Summer School,"The open call is open to anyone who considers themselves a young/starting artist, regardless of age. Prior knowledge or experience with digital media isn’t necessary, but of course welcome! We can host a maximum of 12 participants. If the number of applications exceeds this amount we will make a selection.",Open call – RAIVE AI Summer School,"The open call is open to anyone who considers themselves a young/starting artist, regardless of age. Prior knowledge or experience with digital media isn’t necessary, but of course welcome! We can host a maximum of 12 participants. If the number of applications exceeds this amount we will make a selection.",19 Apr 2026,2026-04-19,2026-09-23 12:37:25.253840+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_28639c301034,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-portraits-miroir-miroir-biennale-de-limage-possible-bip2026/,https://bip-liege.org/en/exhibition/call-for-portraits/,"Biennale de l'Image Possible, BIP2026","The 14th edition of the Biennale de l’Image Possible, BIP2026, will take place in Liège from 17 October to 13 December 2026. Entitled MIROIR MIROIR, it will bring together several exhibitions at a single venue. One will showcase a composite collection of portraits, created from a variety of figures (human and non-human beings) and using any visual medium (painting, photography, video, drawing, etc.). The aim is to create a heterogeneous collection of fragments, free associations arising from a multitude of disparate elements. The selected portraits will be brought together and staged in a vast, free-flowing space. We are soliciting these portraits from you, visual artists. Whether it is a single image or part of a series, large or small, already produced or yet to be produced, painted, drawn or printed, we will consider all your proposals. Self-portraits are permitted, as are group portraits. We are keen to embrace the unique ways in which artists, from all backgrounds, nationalities and generations, have seen, observed and depicted those living individuals who have returned their gaze or granted their presence as a model, an ideal or a subject.",visual artists,call,Belgium,Liège,,,,en,CALL – PORTRAITS – MIROIR MIROIR – Biennale de l’Image Possible – BIP2026,"We are soliciting these portraits from you, visual artists. Whether it is a single image or part of a series, large or small, already produced or yet to be produced, painted, drawn or printed, we will consider all your proposals. Self-portraits are permitted, as are group portraits. We are keen to embrace the unique ways in which artists, from all backgrounds, nationalities and generations, have seen, observed and depicted those living individuals who have returned their gaze or granted their presence as a model, an ideal or a subject.",CALL – PORTRAITS – MIROIR MIROIR – Biennale de l’Image Possible – BIP2026,"We are soliciting these portraits from you, visual artists. Whether it is a single image or part of a series, large or small, already produced or yet to be produced, painted, drawn or printed, we will consider all your proposals. Self-portraits are permitted, as are group portraits. We are keen to embrace the unique ways in which artists, from all backgrounds, nationalities and generations, have seen, observed and depicted those living individuals who have returned their gaze or granted their presence as a model, an ideal or a subject.",19 Apr 2026,2026-04-19,2026-09-23 12:37:25.256844+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_43833eaa836e,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-eco-expo/,https://files.cargocollective.com/c2116640/Sprouts-Eco-Expo-2026---Open-Call.pdf,Sprouts Film Festival,"Sprouts Film Festival (SFF) invites young artists and recent art school graduates whose work revolves around ecological and sustainability themes to apply with their pre-existing work for the Eco Expo, which will take place during the 5th edition of SFF.",artists,open call,,,,,young artists and recent art school graduates,en,Open call – Eco Expo,"Sprouts Film Festival (SFF) invites young artists and recent art school graduates whose work revolves around ecological and sustainability themes to apply with their pre-existing work for the Eco Expo, which will take place during the 5th edition of SFF.

An open call for artists who work with what remains, reshaping archives, objects, or ideas into new ecologies of meaning.",Open call – Eco Expo,"Sprouts Film Festival (SFF) invites young artists and recent art school graduates whose work revolves around ecological and sustainability themes to apply with their pre-existing work for the Eco Expo, which will take place during the 5th edition of SFF.

An open call for artists who work with what remains, reshaping archives, objects, or ideas into new ecologies of meaning.",08 Apr 2026,2026-04-08,2026-09-23 12:37:25.260052+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0d6be3a34e4e,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-festival-performance-pragicomedionale-2026/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeCbZyBypOKxyCFua0yqgFauoF-ilnVKoaBapphrQmOrUjmKQ/viewform,Pragovka Gallery,"Pragovka Gallery announces an open call for participation in the second edition of the Pragicomedionale Performance Festival, which will take place on Saturday, 12 September 2026 at the Pragovka complex.",performance art,open call,Czech and international,Pragovka complex,coverage of travel and accommodation costs where necessary festival PR and production photo documentation printing of posters and accompanying printed materials graphic design of printed materials artist fees (to be specified according to available funding) props and installation materials (please include an estimated budget in the application form),,,en,Open Call Festival Performance Pragicomedionale 2026,The Open Call is open to Czech and international artists. There are no restrictions placed on performers. Applicants may submit any number of performances. The application must include two mandatory attachments: detailed project description the artist’s portfolio and CV / documentation of previous performances Please remember to label all files with the applicant’s name. The size of each file must not exceed 10 MB. Applications that do not meet the above requirements will not be included in the selection process. Files must be submitted exclusively via this form.,Open Call Festival Performance Pragicomedionale 2026,The Open Call is open to Czech and international artists. There are no restrictions placed on performers. Applicants may submit any number of performances. The application must include two mandatory attachments: detailed project description the artist’s portfolio and CV / documentation of previous performances Please remember to label all files with the applicant’s name. The size of each file must not exceed 10 MB. Applications that do not meet the above requirements will not be included in the selection process. Files must be submitted exclusively via this form.,6 April 2026 (23:59),2026-04-06,2026-09-23 12:37:25.264049+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a851810c4e3c,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-hotel-carrousel/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfrOFvLHrIWDp9VWKvSAG0LxmQb5sEQPvi44Xm-E5v8jqgelg/viewform?pli=1,Hotel Carrousel,"Hotel Carrousel is a nomadic exhibition platform dedicated to video and media art, founded in 2024 by artist Lupe Arens.",video and media art,open call,Belgium,Brussels,"Selected artists, duos or collectives will receive a €200 participation fee. Potential production costs are to be discussed upon selection.",,young and emerging artists,en,Open Call – Hotel Carrousel,"Artists, duos and collectives under 35 years old and based in Belgium can apply.",Open Call – Hotel Carrousel,"Artists, duos and collectives under 35 years old and based in Belgium can apply.","March 29, 2026 23:59",2026-03-29,2026-09-23 12:37:25.267742+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_f8fe9857ed58,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/east-call-curatorial-residency/,https://forms.gle/iK4qbDuEgXQzc9Fg9,East Topics,"East Call Curatorial Residency offers a unique opportunity for emerging curators to gain a comprehensive insight in the Hungarian and Slovenian contemporary art scene by examining its characteristics and understanding them in a broader, regional context. East Call is an intensive 2-week program that focuses on the status and practice of artists, contemporary curatorial conditions, institutional situations and the understanding of issues affecting contemporary art, with a focus on the roles and responsibilities of curators as mediators between audiences and artists, and researchers as theoretical transmitters of knowledge, interpretation and contextualization. East Call aims to foster dialogue on issues surrounding curation and to interrogate what constitutes “the curatorial” in the Central Eastern European region. The East Call program focuses on open, horizontal and conversation-based transfers of knowledge and experience.",contemporary art,curatorial residency,Hungary,Budapest,"The fee includes the use of office facilities, participation in workshops, guest lectures, entry fees of museums and special events, the use of public transport in Budapest, inland transport for provincial venues and regional transport for Bratislava.",Participation fee: 1000 EUROS,emerging curators and curators-to-be still involved in their studies,en,East Call Curatorial Residency,The program is designed for emerging curators and curators-to-be still involved in their studies who expect to work in the field of contemporary art.,East Call Curatorial Residency,The program is designed for emerging curators and curators-to-be still involved in their studies who expect to work in the field of contemporary art.,27 March 2026,2026-03-27,2026-09-23 12:37:25.270810+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_780119e0d51f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/high-fest-international-performing-arts-festival-open-call-2/,https://highfest.am/apply/,HIGH FEST,"Register for the 24th edition of HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival! HIGH FEST is delighted to announce the opening of registrations for the 24th edition of the HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival, which will take place from 1 to 8 October 2026 in Yerevan, Armenia.",Performing Arts,Festival,Armenia,Yerevan,,,,en,HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival – Open Call,Fill in the attached registration form. Send it to: administration@highfest.am,HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival – Open Call,Fill in the attached registration form. Send it to: administration@highfest.am,15 Mar 2026,2026-03-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.274004+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2c5ed7b40a1d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/european-media-art-platform-residency-programme-2026/,,European Media Art Platform (EMAP),"European Media Art Platform (EMAP) returns in 2026 with a residency programme for artists and collectives in 15 countries. EMAP invites artists, artist duos, collectives, and artistic collaborations working in digital, media, robotic, and bio art to apply for a two-month production residency in 2026.","digital, media, robotic, and bio art",residency programme,"Austria, France, Slovakia, Portugal, Belgium, The Netherlands, Slovenia, Croatia, Spain, Italy, Cyprus, Greece, Latvia, Germany, Poland","Linz, Marseille, Košice, Braga, Brussels, Utrecht, Ljubljana, Zagreb, Gijón, Milan, Limassol, Athens, Riga, Halle (Saale), Wrocław","4,000 EUR grant
2,000 EUR grant for collaborating artist(s)
4,000 EUR project budget
Accommodation provided by host
Travel expenses
Access to technical facilities and/or media labs",,PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.,en,European Media Art Platform Residency Programme 2026,"Applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state, or residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries. Undergraduate and Master’s students are not eligible. PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.",European Media Art Platform Residency Programme 2026,"Applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state, or residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries. Undergraduate and Master’s students are not eligible. PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.",13 Mar 2026,2026-03-13,2026-09-23 12:37:25.278216+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_28881ec0704a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ape-camp-2026-open-call-for-overseas-artists-producers-and-engineers/,,Arts Council Korea (ARKO),"Arts Council Korea (ARKO) invites artists, producers, and engineers aged 39 or under from around the world to APE CAMP 2026. The program aims to nurture creative talent and activate sustainable networks for the convergence of art and technology. Through the camp, participants are supported in developing new ideas and building global networks.","Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc.; technology fields related to art–technology convergence",camp,Republic of Korea,Seoul or Gyeonggi,Round-trip airfare (partial support) Accommodation during the camp period (based on shared rooms for two) Meals during the camp period,Free of charge,Young artists and producers aged 39 or under; Preference will be given to early-career technology professionals.,en,"APE CAMP 2026: Open call for overseas artists, producers and engineers","General (mandatory) Applications must be submitted by individuals only. This open call is for international participants who do not hold Korean nationality. Participants must be able to attend all programs during the camp period from 12 to 16 June 2026. (※ Selection will be cancelled if a participant withdraws after selection or attends only part of the program.) Applicants must be able to communicate in English. Art category (Mandatory) Young artists and producers aged 39 or under who are actively engaged in creative practices related to art–technology convergence Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc. Technology category (Mandatory) Professionals, researchers, and experts in technology fields who possess specialised knowledge applicable to art–technology convergence–based creative practices. The eligible technology fields include, but are not limited to, the areas listed below. Applicants working in other relevant technology fields not listed may also apply.","APE CAMP 2026: Open call for overseas artists, producers and engineers","General (mandatory) Applications must be submitted by individuals only. This open call is for international participants who do not hold Korean nationality. Participants must be able to attend all programs during the camp period from 12 to 16 June 2026. (※ Selection will be cancelled if a participant withdraws after selection or attends only part of the program.) Applicants must be able to communicate in English. Art category (Mandatory) Young artists and producers aged 39 or under who are actively engaged in creative practices related to art–technology convergence Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc. Technology category (Mandatory) Professionals, researchers, and experts in technology fields who possess specialised knowledge applicable to art–technology convergence–based creative practices. The eligible technology fields include, but are not limited to, the areas listed below. Applicants working in other relevant technology fields not listed may also apply.","Thursday, 12 March 2026, 23:59 KST",2026-03-12,2026-09-23 12:37:25.285857+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_8a344b3ec711,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-met-kunstenpunt-naar-classicalnext-in-budapest/,,Flanders Arts Institute & WBM,"From 8 to 11 April Classical:NEXT , an international meeting for the classical music sector with a conference, a fair and a showcase programme, will take place in Budapest. Flanders Arts Institute will once again coordinate our sector’s presence together with Wallonie-Bruxelles Musiques (WBM). Classical:NEXT is the main international gathering for classical music innovation in Europe. As always, we are looking forward to being part of this event again and highlighting our classical music. Want to join Flanders Arts Institute?",classical music,open call,Hungary,Budapest,€ 400 per person enrolled who does not receive an operational subsidy € 200 per registered person for those receiving an operating subsidy of less than €150000,,,en,Join Flanders Arts Institute at Classical:NEXT in Budapest,"Are you eligible for this extra financial support? If so, please contact Ward Bosmans after you registered.",Join Flanders Arts Institute at Classical:NEXT in Budapest,"Are you eligible for this extra financial support? If so, please contact Ward Bosmans after you registered.",08 Mar 2026,2026-03-08,2026-09-23 12:37:25.288806+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_78c404ddf0fa,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-par-hasard-2/,,Par Hasard,"On May 23, Par Hasard is organizing ‘ Par Hasard x Giftshop ‘ together with Giftshop. We invite audiences to come and nose into the cooking pots of artists. Spectators do not always get the opportunity to get an insight into the whole process that leads to a final performance or show. And that is exactly what we want to change. Through this open call we would like to invite makers, performers, musicians, poets, dancers… to apply to participate in this Par Hasard edition. The idea is to give you the opportunity to show your work-in-progress in simple, clear and appropriate context. You can present your work-in-progress to a wide audience in order to take the next step in the creation process.",performing arts,open call,Belgium,,Travel expenses from countries outside of Belgium cannot be reimbursed.,,,en,Open Call Par Hasard,For who – You have a degree in the arts or relevant experience in the arts sector – you share a work-in-progress or an experiment (max 15min) – your work is suitable for the location (limited technical resources) – your work-in-progress should have a performative character,Open Call Par Hasard,For who – You have a degree in the arts or relevant experience in the arts sector – you share a work-in-progress or an experiment (max 15min) – your work is suitable for the location (limited technical resources) – your work-in-progress should have a performative character,06 Mar 2026,2026-03-06,2026-09-23 12:37:25.292617+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_37a488364201,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-international-young-artists-presentation-iyap-2026/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfbckxMMwUyOIEt9jPYq85X8sRl7DhctVu7zjA_dNot4U0iiw/viewform?usp=dialog,Musica & AMUZ (Flanders Festival Antwerp),International Young Artist’s Presentation (IYAP) 2026 offers you a unique platform to shine in front of an international audience and professionals from the sector.,vocal and/or instrumental musicians and ensembles,presentation,Belgium,Antwerp,,There is no registration fee; only travel and accommodation costs are covered by the ensembles themselves.,Young,en,OPEN CALL: International Young Artist’s Presentation (IYAP) 2026,Who is it for? Young vocal and/or instrumental musicians and ensembles with a maximum average age of 35. The ensemble focuses on playing historical instruments or using historical sources (up to 1920). A condition for participation is that the entire ensemble must be available and present from August 18 to 22.,OPEN CALL: International Young Artist’s Presentation (IYAP) 2026,Who is it for? Young vocal and/or instrumental musicians and ensembles with a maximum average age of 35. The ensemble focuses on playing historical instruments or using historical sources (up to 1920). A condition for participation is that the entire ensemble must be available and present from August 18 to 22.,01 Mar 2026,2026-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.295631+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_3aeeb0c33c84,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-showcase-emerging-sound-2026/,https://www.stuk.be/en/program/open-call-showcase-emerging-sound-2026,"Q-02, STUK, Musica & C-TAKT","STUK, Q-O2, Musica and C-TAKT present an annual showcase of emerging sound artists in Belgium. The showcase shines a light on the diversity of the Belgian sound art landscape, and gives a boost to an upcoming generation of makers. We are looking for recent, existing sound work in any format: performance, installation, soundwalk, radio piece, intervention or other formats.",sound art,Open call,Belgium,null,,,emerging,en,Open Call showcase Emerging Sound 2026,"For whom? You are an emerging sound artist. In other words: in training, recently graduated, at the start of a career or still in need of developing a network within the Belgian or international sound art field. You make sound-based work such as installation, performance, soundwalk, participatory work, radio art or intervention in public space. You are asked to propose only one existing work or work-in-progress that is not older than 2024. Submissions with more than one work will not be considered. You have a link to Belgium: either by residence, education or nationality.",Open Call showcase Emerging Sound 2026,"For whom? You are an emerging sound artist. In other words: in training, recently graduated, at the start of a career or still in need of developing a network within the Belgian or international sound art field. You make sound-based work such as installation, performance, soundwalk, participatory work, radio art or intervention in public space. You are asked to propose only one existing work or work-in-progress that is not older than 2024. Submissions with more than one work will not be considered. You have a link to Belgium: either by residence, education or nationality.",01 Mar 2026,2026-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.299725+00:00
