kunsten_be_flanders_b363b1956897,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/sofam-beurzen-2025-6/,,SOFAM,"We are delighted to announce our new call for SOFAM Grants 2025/6. For this edition, a professional jury will award 20 grants. If you are selected, you will receive €2,500 to invest in your practice, plus possible publication in a future SOFAM Revue.",visual artists,grants,Belgium,,"20 grants... you will receive €2,500 to invest in your practice, plus possible publication in a future SOFAM Revue.",,professional,en,SOFAM Grants 2025/6,"The SOFAM grants are destined for professional visual artists in Belgium, who are a member of SOFAM or who plan to join. Are you already a member of another collective management society in Belgium for visual work? Then, unfortunately, this call is not for you.",SOFAM Grants 2025/6,"The SOFAM grants are destined for professional visual artists in Belgium, who are a member of SOFAM or who plan to join. Are you already a member of another collective management society in Belgium for visual work? Then, unfortunately, this call is not for you.",28 Dec 2025,2025-12-28,2026-09-23 12:37:25.403068+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d4dcb3347320,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/imal-ipo-call-for-residencies-2026/,https://www.imal.org/en/events/ipo26,iMAL,"iMAL Project Office is an open call aimed at artists and creators based in Belgium. Through residencies of maximum one month at iMAL, we seek to provide production & research assistance to support and develop new artistic projects. The 2026 iPO programme: LABOR-atorium – a co-creation research residency with LABoral (Gijón, SP) Stages – a residency co-organised with A Two Dogs Company (Brussels) Fablab Experiments – two residencies at Fablab iMAL",artists and creators,Residency,Belgium,,production & research assistance,,,en,iMAL iPO call for residencies 2026,an open call aimed at artists and creators based in Belgium.,iMAL iPO call for residencies 2026,an open call aimed at artists and creators based in Belgium.,22 Dec 2025,2025-12-22,2026-09-23 12:37:25.406324+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_e4a2cb6c28a5,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-op-residentie-bij-a-two-dogs-company-imal/,https://www.imal.org/en/events/ipo26/stages,iMAL and A Two Dogs Company,"STAGES is an annual residency programme initiated by iMAL and A Two Dogs Company. They are looking for artists who wish to work at the confluence of performing arts and digital arts, with transversal projects that fully take advantage of both the black box of the performance stage, and the white cube of the exhibition space. iMAL and ATDC aim in particular to support the development of projects in which technical elements play an essential role. The residency aims to help you tackle these technical and dramaturgical challenges, with both organisations sharing their resources and expertise in their respective fields. The residency will take place at the A Two Dogs Company atelier/studio and the iMAL spaces and lab.",performing arts and digital arts,residency,Belgium,,,,emerging artists,en,Open Call residency at A Two Dogs Company & iMAL,"This call is aimed at emerging artists. Applicants must be resident in Belgium, regardless of nationality, gender, religion or ethnic origin. They strongly encourage candidates of all origins and identities to apply. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works.",Open Call residency at A Two Dogs Company & iMAL,"This call is aimed at emerging artists. Applicants must be resident in Belgium, regardless of nationality, gender, religion or ethnic origin. They strongly encourage candidates of all origins and identities to apply. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works.",22 Dec 2025,2025-12-22,2026-09-23 12:37:25.409297+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_e2c3698c1650,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-prix-la-puissance-du-lien-by-sakura-2026-edition/,https://www.lapuissancedulien.org/prix/le-prix-de-la-puissance-du-lien-par-sakura,Sakura Fund,"The prize invites participants to explore, through their lens, the many faces of human and social connection.",Photography,prize,,,"Seven prizes will be awarded, for a total of €4,000, funded by the Sakura Fund, with the support of GRK for printing and the catalogue.",,Youth (12–25 years old) ; Over 25 (amateur or professional),en,Open Call – Prix La Puissance du Lien by Sakura (2026 Edition),"• Youth (12–25 years old)
