arts_council_wales_32942d1388ee,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/research-and-development-0,https://arts.wales/application-process,Arts Council of Wales,Research and Development supports the development and creation of high-quality and ambitious work. It supports exploring and developing new ideas and ways of working in collaboration with partners. Proposals should have a clear intention to create work that will reach audiences and demonstrate a strong potential for future success.,the artforms that we support,funding,Wales,,"There are two levels of award: small, up to £10,000 and large, up to £30,000.",,,en,Research and Development,"Organisations and individuals can apply. Take a look at our eligibility criteria for organisations and our eligibility criteria for individuals to see if you are eligible. Please note - For individuals looking to develop their own practice rather than to develop work with intent to reach audiences, please see our Creative Practice fund .",Research and Development,"Organisations and individuals can apply. Take a look at our eligibility criteria for organisations and our eligibility criteria for individuals to see if you are eligible. Please note - For individuals looking to develop their own practice rather than to develop work with intent to reach audiences, please see our Creative Practice fund .",,,2026-09-23 13:53:09.926321+00:00
arts_council_wales_ccdc0a35b8b6,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/international/international-opportunities-fund,https://portal.arts.wales/,Arts Council of Wales / Wales Arts International,Funding for the development and delivery of international work.,arts,funding,Wales,,"Up to £7,500 for: International Collaboration and International Partnership Development International Presentation of Work International Networks and Events Up to £5,000 for: International Residencies For international residencies taking place outside of Europe and in locations where travel and living costs might be higher, we may be able to accept an application requesting support up to a maximum of £7,500.",,,en,International Opportunities Fund,Arts organisations and individual creative professionals based in Wales.  Individuals and organisations based in Wales and working within the artforms we support .,International Opportunities Fund,Arts organisations and individual creative professionals based in Wales.  Individuals and organisations based in Wales and working within the artforms we support .,,,2026-09-23 13:53:09.926333+00:00
arts_council_wales_2c1de1c8af81,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/four-nations-international-fund,https://my.creativescotland.com/login,"Arts Council England, Arts Council Northern Ireland, Arts Council of Wales / Wales Arts International and Creative Scotland",the third round of the Four Nations International Fund invites applications from artists and creative practitioners across the UK who wish to work with partners in Europe and beyond.,artists and creative practitioners,funding,"England, Northern Ireland, Scotland, and Wales",,"With a total budget of £335,000, this round offers up to £7,500 per project.",,,en,Four Nations International Fund,"Open to artists, creative practitioners and organisations based in England, Northern Ireland, Scotland, and Wales, the funding is designed for those seeking to collaborate with both counterparts in the other UK nations, along with those internationally to share ideas, co‑create, and reach new audiences.",Four Nations International Fund,"Open to artists, creative practitioners and organisations based in England, Northern Ireland, Scotland, and Wales, the funding is designed for those seeking to collaborate with both counterparts in the other UK nations, along with those internationally to share ideas, co‑create, and reach new audiences.","2pm, Wednesday 25 February 2026",2026-02-25,2026-09-23 13:53:09.930437+00:00
can_serrat_217dbea20ea5,can_serrat,https://canserrat.org/writers-residency-open-call-2027,https://forms.gle/TkNsHb6W9mmTWFj98,Can Serrat,Can Serrat is opening a new residency call for writers from all backgrounds and nationalities.,writers,residency,Spain,El Bruc,Invitations: Full Grant for two months Full Grant for one month 30 Partial Grants,,,en,SUMMER – AUTUMN 2027 OPEN CALL for WRITERS at CAN SERRAT,Can Serrat is opening a new residency call for writers from all backgrounds and nationalities.,SUMMER – AUTUMN 2027 OPEN CALL for WRITERS at CAN SERRAT,Can Serrat is opening a new residency call for writers from all backgrounds and nationalities.,"September 1st to the 23rd, 2026",2027-09-01,2026-09-23 13:53:09.958626+00:00
can_serrat_c72d67f59662,can_serrat,https://canserrat.org/en-visual-art-residency-open-call-2027,https://forms.gle/p4w5bv4rCc71L8Zs5,Can Serrat,"Can Serrat is opening a new residency call for visual and multidisciplinary artists from all backgrounds and nationalities. The residencies will take place during summer and autumn 2027 in El Bruc, at the foot of Montserrat and 45 km from Barcelona.",visual and multidisciplinary art,residency,Spain,El Bruc,"Invitations: Full Grant for six weeks + artist fee Full Grant for one month 20 Partial Grants

Full Grant + artist fee:
● Accommodation at Can Serrat (private room for six weeks from 2nd of August 2027).
● Meals: 2 prepared community dinners per week, access to a list of basic food supplies (coffee, tea, condiments, and some dry goods depending on availability).
● Artist Fee 2000€, subject to the receipt of the totality public funding.

Full Grant:
● Accommodation at Can Serrat (shared room for one month in October 2027).
● Meals: 2 prepared community dinners per week, access to a list of basic food supplies (coffee, tea, condiments, and some dry goods depending on availability).

Partial Grants: Minimum residency duration: one month
● Option 1 Shared room: €1130/month (shared with up to 3 people)
● Option 2 Private room: €1745/month
● Option 3 Studio only (no accommodation or meals included): €305/month
*Options 1 and 2 include 2 prepared community dinners, access to a list of basic food items (coffee, tea, condiments, and some dry goods, depending on availability).

Production Grant — Visual Arts
Financial support of €3,000* intended to recognize one of the artistic processes developed during the residency and support its future production.

Retorns Grants — Visual Arts and Writing
Return grant to come back to Can Serrat for an additional one-month residency during the following year.",,,en,OPEN CALL SUMMER – AUTUMN 2027_VISUAL AND MULTIDISCIPLINARY ARTISTS,The residency call for visual and multidisciplinary artists from all backgrounds and nationalities.,OPEN CALL SUMMER – AUTUMN 2027_VISUAL AND MULTIDISCIPLINARY ARTISTS,The residency call for visual and multidisciplinary artists from all backgrounds and nationalities.,"Application Period: September 1st to the 23rd, 2026",2027-09-01,2026-09-23 13:53:09.966955+00:00
can_serrat_bda1091bdb89,can_serrat,https://canserrat.org/collective-creation2027_internationalresidency,https://forms.gle/KxfqCEwRnwvGfqNNA,Can Serrat,"These laboratory-format residencies invite artists, writers, and researchers from diverse disciplines to explore walking as an artistic and research methodology through an intensive process of collective work situated within the landscape of Montserrat.","artists, writers, and researchers from diverse disciplines",Art Residency Program,,,"Thanks to the support of the Department of Culture, participants benefit from a reduced participation fee.",,,en,Collective Creation Laboratory 2027,"People of any background and age (minors with authorization). It is not necessary to be an artist or writer. The laboratory welcomes anyone interested in research, creative practice, and collaborative ways of working. Individual, duo, or collective applications are accepted. Group Residencies The Collective Creation programme is designed to support creative processes developed through collaboration, exchange, and shared research. We welcome artistic collectives, research groups, and other collaborative initiatives. To encourage collective participation and respond to the specific needs of group-based processes, we offer dedicated conditions for applications from groups of 4 or more participants attending the residency during the same period.",Collective Creation Laboratory 2027,"People of any background and age (minors with authorization). It is not necessary to be an artist or writer. The laboratory welcomes anyone interested in research, creative practice, and collaborative ways of working. Individual, duo, or collective applications are accepted. Group Residencies The Collective Creation programme is designed to support creative processes developed through collaboration, exchange, and shared research. We welcome artistic collectives, research groups, and other collaborative initiatives. To encourage collective participation and respond to the specific needs of group-based processes, we offer dedicated conditions for applications from groups of 4 or more participants attending the residency during the same period.","Application period: March 27 – October 3, 2026.",2027-03-27,2026-09-23 13:53:09.977091+00:00
deutscher_uebersetzerfonds_fd2461c9db20,deutscher_uebersetzerfonds,https://www.uebersetzerfonds.de/files/Workshop_post-kolonial_afriCOLOGNE.pdf,,africologneFESTIVAL,Das africologneFESTIVAL lädt im Herbst 2026 zu einem dreitägigen Workshop für post-koloniale Theaterübersetzung nach Köln ein.,Theaterübersetzung,Workshop,Germany,Köln,Die Teilnahme am Workshop ist kostenfrei. Für Verpflegung und Vorstellungsbesuch fallen insgesamt 30 € an.,Die Teilnahme am Workshop ist kostenfrei. Für Verpflegung und Vorstellungsbesuch fallen insgesamt 30 € an.,,de,Workshop „Post-koloniale Theaterübersetzung“,"Er richtet sich an Übersetzer*innen, Theatermacher*innen und kulturpolitisch Interessierte aus NRW, die sich mit den besonderen Herausforderungen der Übersetzung afrikanischer und afrodiasporischer Dramatik auseinandersetzen möchten. Besonders willkommen sind BIPOC-Bewerber*innen sowie Personen mit unterschiedlichen Hintergründen in Übersetzung, Theaterpraxis, Aktivismus oder Kulturkritik. Englisch- und Französischkenntnisse sind willkommen. Noch wichtiger ist jedoch die Bereitschaft zur kollektiven Arbeit und zur kritischen Auseinandersetzung mit Sprache, Macht und Repräsentation.",Workshop “Postcolonial Theatre Translation”,"It is aimed at translators, theatre practitioners, and those interested in cultural policy from NRW who would like to engage with the particular challenges of translating African and Afrodiasporic drama. BIPOC applicants as well as people with diverse backgrounds in translation, theatre practice, activism, or cultural criticism are especially welcome. Knowledge of English and French is welcome. However, even more important is the willingness to work collectively and to engage critically with language, power, and representation.",bis zum 5. September,2027-09-05,2026-09-23 13:53:11.774816+00:00
