norwegian_crafts_05470dd4cbeb,norwegian_crafts,https://norwegiancrafts.no/opportunities/monumental-crafts,https://konsthantverkscentrum.se/?p=51875&preview=1&_ppp=d18c3ce290,Ifö Center and Konsthantverkscentrum,"Monumental Crafts is a project dedicated to highlighting, presenting, and sharing knowledge about professional contemporary craft, with a focus on large-scale work. The project includes a group exhibition featuring 15 artists from Sweden, Norway, and Denmark, alongside a residency for three craft makers seeking to work in larger formats and spaces.",craft,group exhibition and artist residency,Norway,,"Financial Support: Material budget included + 1,000 SEK weekly stipend. Solo Exhibition Fee: 16,320 SEK (+ VAT) per artist in accordance with the MU Agreement, plus covered freight and travel expenses. Artist Fee: 5,000 SEK (+ VAT) per artist, paid in accordance with the MU Agreement.",,,en,"Open Call: Monumental Crafts, Ifö Center Group exhibition and Artist Residency","Norway-based craft artists are invited to apply for Monumental Crafts, a major Nordic collaboration between Konsthantverkscentrum and Ifö Center (Sweden).","Open Call: Monumental Crafts, Ifö Center Group exhibition and Artist Residency","Norway-based craft artists are invited to apply for Monumental Crafts, a major Nordic collaboration between Konsthantverkscentrum and Ifö Center (Sweden).",15 October 2026 (23:59 CET),2026-10-15,2026-09-23 13:55:14.775788+00:00
