rannis_iceland_8c97d0bb99e2,rannis_iceland,https://en.rannis.is/funding/art-culture/support-for-the-publication-of-books-in-icelandic/,https://sjodir.rannis.is/menu/api/oauth2_callback.php,The Icelandic Centre for Research,To support the publication of books in Icelandic by providing temporary financial aid to publishers in the form of a partial reimbursement of costs incurred in the publication of books in Icelandic.,Art and Culture,support,Iceland,Reykjavík,"The 25% reimbursement only pertains to costs related to the publication of a book, costs without VAT.",,,en,Support for the publication of books in Icelandic,"Target group Book publishers, i.e. an individual, group or legal person financially responsible for the publication of a book, registered as a party subject to value added tax pursuant to Article 5 of the Value Added Tax Act, No 50/1988, under code 58.11.0 Book publishing according to the classification of economic activities published by Statistics Iceland. Foreign applicants mustprovide evidence of similar registration of their activities in another country.",Support for the publication of books in Icelandic,"Target group Book publishers, i.e. an individual, group or legal person financially responsible for the publication of a book, registered as a party subject to value added tax pursuant to Article 5 of the Value Added Tax Act, No 50/1988, under code 58.11.0 Book publishing according to the classification of economic activities published by Statistics Iceland. Foreign applicants mustprovide evidence of similar registration of their activities in another country.",Open for applications all year round. An application must be received no later than nine months after the publication of the book concerned.,2027-06-23,2026-09-23 13:55:18.318829+00:00
roberto_cimetta_fund_23ba036056c8,roberto_cimetta_fund,https://www.cimettafund.org/en/blog/2026/09/22/emergency-mobility-grants-2027-roberto-cimetta-fund-opens-an-emergency-call/,https://www.cimettafund.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RCF-Emergency-Mobility-Grants-2027-Application-Form-EN.docx,Roberto Cimetta Fund,"The Roberto Cimetta Fund is opening a call to fund professional travel for artists and cultural professionals from Lebanon, Syria, Palestine, Yemen and Sudan.",performing arts and multidisciplinary practices,grant,,,"Each grant can reach €600 and covers international and national travel, visa and consular processing fees, and a basic daily allowance.",,"If you are at the start of your career and do not have a body of work yet, showing the project you are working on now is enough.",en,Emergency Mobility Grants 2027,"The call is open to artists and cultural professionals from Lebanon, Syria, Palestine, Yemen and Sudan, whether they live in those countries or come from them and live elsewhere. Individual artists and constituted groups are both eligible. Cultural structures can take part only as hosts or inviting partners, within a professional collaboration. There is no age limit. The call is restricted to performing arts and multidisciplinary practices. Three types of activity are supported: professional training, creation and residency, dissemination and networking.",Emergency Mobility Grants 2027,"The call is open to artists and cultural professionals from Lebanon, Syria, Palestine, Yemen and Sudan, whether they live in those countries or come from them and live elsewhere. Individual artists and constituted groups are both eligible. Cultural structures can take part only as hosts or inviting partners, within a professional collaboration. There is no age limit. The call is restricted to performing arts and multidisciplinary practices. Three types of activity are supported: professional training, creation and residency, dissemination and networking.",1 November 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 13:55:18.322318+00:00
